# Challenges – Sprint 28

## Challenges Faced

### Challenge 1

Identifying how the current Salesforce User could be connected to the correct `Student__c` record.

### Solution

Created a `Student_User__c` Lookup(User) field on the `Student__c` object and connected the Student record with the Salesforce User.

---

### Challenge 2

There was no existing Student Controller or Student Service to identify the current student's record.

### Solution

Created a `StudentProfileController` Apex class that uses the logged-in Salesforce User to find the related `Student__c` record.

---

### Challenge 3

Understanding how to update the Student record without creating unnecessary custom update logic.

### Solution

Used Lightning Data Service with `lightning-record-edit-form` to display and update the Student record.

---

### Challenge 4

Adding the Student Profile component to the existing application.

### Solution

Added the `StudentProfile` component to the existing Eligible Jobs Lightning App Builder page instead of creating a separate page.

---

### Challenge 5

Testing whether the profile information was actually saved after submitting the form.

### Solution

Deployed the changes and tested the form in Salesforce. After submitting the form, the message **"Profile updated successfully"** was displayed, confirming that the update was successful.
